    {
      "id": "87f64d16-9cf8-48bf-bbe4-1542954e23b1",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 327,
      "shortId": "J34RD",
      "priority": 4,
      "shortName": "show-layer-actions",
      "title": "ShowLayer / HideLayer on-demand layers → a first native exposé",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "Migration step 3. `ShowLayer(id)` makes an OnDemand layer visible and active, so the base context goes dormant when it is a context switch. A keybinding maps to it like any action, so it is rebindable and reachable from mouse and RPC.\n\n## ✅ DECIDED 2026-08-04 — how a plugin updates a layer it already owns\n\nThe question arose from T339: `open_view_layer` realizes **once**, at open, so it was unclear whether the retained `ViewNode` is load-bearing. Four options were put to Antonio; he chose **signals — the plugin never resends the tree.**\n\n**The mechanism is P085(F003)/T360** (`58SE7`, \"A component's own signals: a per-mount value store a plugin can write\"), which already specifies it: a `(mount, key) → Signal<PropValue>` map on `SharedChromeState`, and — its step 5 — a `ViewNode` that can **name a value key instead of a literal**, so the realized widget binds the signal and updates **in place** with no tree rebuild. Its own open question (the prop spelling: a `PropValue::Binding(String)` versus a `PropValue::Text(\"@key\")` sigil) is still Antonio's to settle.\n\n**Rejected, with reasons:**\n- *Replace on update* (`update_view(id, node)` → re-realize and swap) — throws the retained tree away, so caret, selection, scroll, focus and `FormBindings` all die with it. **Do not add `update_view` to `LayerRegistry`**: it would be a second update channel that T360 would then have to kill.\n- *Diff and reconcile* — preserves everything, but a reconciler has no precedent in this codebase and would be the largest thing in the plugin path. Not until something demands it.\n- *Immutable layers in v1* — was the recommended stepping stone; Antonio chose to go to the signal model directly instead.\n\n**Unaffected either way:** a theme reload can re-realize from the retained node. That is what the node on `LayerContent::View` earns today, independent of plugin updates.\n\n## Consequence for this task\n\nT327 needs a **native** exposé, which updates nothing, so nothing here is blocked by T360. Build `ShowLayer`/`HideLayer` against the registry's existing `show()`/`hide()` (`heca/src/chrome/layers.rs:172`, documented as \"`ShowLayer` dispatches here\") and do **not** invent an update path along the way.\n\n## State on 2026-08-04\n\nSet `in-progress` only to carry the T339 follow-up correction (commit `966e484`: `LayerContent::View(ViewNode)` restored to the ratified §9 shape, realized tree moved to `DynamicLayer.realized`). **T327's own work — the actions — has not started.**",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [
        {
          "id": "87f64d16-9cf8-48bf-bbe4-1542954e23b1-check-001-planned-in-progress",
          "date": "2026-08-04T20:16:52.186Z",
