    {
      "id": "fe6f4b88-4cd7-4c0b-8f04-53c1bc03937e",
      "phaseId": "5464ff74-fa17-4412-abaa-95aa19810b33",
      "number": 339,
      "shortId": "PQADT",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "layer-content-viewnode",
      "title": "Add LayerContent with the View(ViewNode) arm",
      "status": "done",
      "description": "`heca/src/chrome/layers.rs` has `LayerBand` and `LayerKind` but no `LayerContent` — a layer holds a native tree and nothing can hand it a description. Add `LayerContent::{Native(Box<dyn Component>), View(ViewNode)}` and realize the View arm through the ONE bridge (heca/src/chrome/realize.rs). Occluder comes from the realized tree's laid-out bounds — NEVER hardcoded.\n\n---\n**Completion summary:**\nDone 2026-08-04. `heca/src/chrome/layers.rs` + `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs`.\n\n## What shipped\n\n- **`LayerContent`** with both arms: `Native(Box<dyn Component>)` and `View { node, realized }`. `DynamicLayer.root` became `content: LayerContent`, with `root()` / `root_mut()` accessors so every consumer is arm-agnostic.\n- **`LayerRegistry::add_view(band, kind, modal, covers_content, node, realized)`** — the View-arm constructor, mirroring `add`.\n- **`chrome::overlay::open_view_layer(state, band, kind, modal, covers_content, node)`** — the host entry point. Realizes through the **one** bridge (`super::realize` → `heca_view_realize::realize`) with the same boundary `build_modal_root` uses: a `ViewHintTargets` sink so the described tree's buttons are KeyHint-reachable, and an emitter that wraps the model's own `Intent` into `InteractionIntent::View` at the edge.\n\n## Design decision — the View arm keeps BOTH the node and the realized tree\n\nThe task's literal signature was `View(ViewNode)`. It is `View { node, realized }` instead, for two reasons:\n\n1. **A registry cannot realize.** `realize(node, theme, emit, hints, forms)` needs the theme, an intent emitter, the hint sink and the form bindings; `LayerRegistry` is plain data on `AppState` and holds none of them. So the caller realizes and hands both over — which is why `open_view_layer` exists at all.\n2. **Keeping only the tree would throw the description away.** The node is the source of truth a theme reload or a plugin update re-realizes from; the tree is what the host lays out, paints and hint-walks. `LayerContent::node()` exposes it, and the test asserts it survives realization.\n\n## The occluder invariant holds\n\nNothing is hardcoded and nothing was added: `active_hint_targets` (`heca/src/chrome/mod.rs:2182`) reads `layer.root().base().bounds`, so a View layer's occluder is its **realized tree's laid-out bounds** by construction — it goes through the same accessor as a native one.\n\n## Verification\n\n1151 tests, clippy 0 warnings. New test `a_view_layer_behaves_like_any_other_and_keeps_its_description`: a described layer sorts by band beside a native one, declares coverage the same way, keeps its `ViewNode`, and a native layer offers no description — the arms are not interchangeable.\n\n## Follow-on\n\n`open_view_layer` has **no caller yet** — it is a seam, which is why `layers.rs` still carries `#![allow(dead_code)]`. Its first consumer is **P082(F003)/T327** (`ShowLayer` / `HideLayer` actions → the native exposé): the registry's `show()`/`hide()` already exist and are documented as \"`ShowLayer` dispatches here\", but no `WmAction` reaches them.\n\nNot verified visually — nothing renders through this path until T327 gives it a caller.",
      "notes": "",
      "statusLog": [],
      "decisions": [],
      "acceptedDecisions": [],
