  "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T20:26:21.953Z",
  "handoff": "# P082 handoff — 2026-08-06 (the exposé, and the framework bugs it exposed)\n\n## State\n\nBranch `feat/palette-modes`. Last commit `fc9c18b`. **1189 tests, clippy 0 warnings** (the only line\nis `block v0.1.6`'s future-incompat note, from a dependency).\n\n⚠️ **NOTHING IS COMMITTED.** ~30 files are modified in the working tree. Antonio's standing rule:\n**never commit unless asked.** Do not commit to \"clean up\".\n\nModified: `config.default.toml`, `heca-config/src/settings.rs`, `heca-core/src/layout/{session,types}.rs`,\n`heca-grid-ui/src/{component,effects,lib}.rs`, `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/{button,card_grid,dialog,input,mod,row,scroll_region}.rs`,\n`heca-grid-ui/tests/{phase_a,prop_drift}.rs`, `heca-theme/src/theme.rs`, `heca-view/src/{build,lib}.rs`,\n`heca-view-realize/src/lib.rs`, `heca/src/app/{events,focus,interaction,lifecycle,mutations,render,startup}.rs`,\n`heca/src/app_state.rs`, `heca/src/chrome/{expose,layers,mod}.rs`, `heca/src/providers/workspaces/mod.rs`.\n\n## 🔴 START HERE\n\n**`P084(F004)/T394` (`X7SSB`) — \"A real pointer/event vocabulary on Base, and context menus declared\non the widget\".** Written 2026-08-06 with every decision, the code example Antonio wrote, the\n`file:line` evidence, seven edge cases and a 14-item checklist. Antonio said *\"now implement it all.\nAnd write full detailed documentation after coded.\"* That is the next work. **Read T394 in full\nbefore touching anything** — it is the design record, not a summary.\n\nOne question was put to him and is **unanswered**: land the routing change (checklist 1–5) first so\nhe can drive it, or do the whole thing in one pass. Ask again; do not assume.\n\nThere is **one leftover compile error to clear first**: an unfinished test\n`every_row_kind_carries_a_nav_key_the_hit_test_can_find` in `heca/src/providers/workspaces/mod.rs`\n(~line 1450) calls `SharedChromeState::default()`, which does not exist. Either find the real\nconstructor or delete the test. `cargo test -p heca --bins` currently fails to compile because of it.\n(The *fix* it guards is already in and working — see below.)\n\n---\n\n## What this session changed, and why\n\n### The exposé (T327) — now working end to end\n\n`prefix+Tab` opens it. Enter/Space/click choose a pane; Escape/`q`/`Ctrl+q` close it.\n\n**niri's model, verified against `src/layout/monitor.rs` (fetched from the repo, not guessed):**\n\n```rust\nfn workspace_size(zoom) = view_size * zoom          // a row IS the screen, scaled\nfn workspace_gap(zoom)  = view_size.h * 0.1 * zoom  // gap = a tenth of a screen\nstatic_offset = (view_size - ws_size) / 2\nfirst_ws_y    = -active_ws_idx * ws_height_with_gap\nzoom          = 1 - progress * (1 - zoom_setting)   // opens by zooming OUT from life size\n```\n\n**But Antonio overrode part of it after seeing it (2026-08-05): centre the CARD THE CURSOR IS ON,\nnot the workspace rectangle.** niri centres the workspace rectangle; heca centres the selected pane,\non both axes, unclamped (`overscroll(true)`), because *\"the selected pane is centered even if it is\nthe leftmost\"*. Do not \"restore fidelity\" to niri here — this was tried and rejected. The\n`RevealWindow` widget and `Component::reveal_rect` built for the rectangle model were **reverted**;\ndo not reintroduce them.\n\nSettled about the map:\n- No workspace-name gutter. A fixed label column pushed every strip inwards so a row stopped lining\n  up with the screen it pictures; niri labels nothing either.\n- Row gap and zoom come from `LayoutOptions.overview_gap` / `.overview_scale`, exposed as\n  `[settings] overview_gap` (0.1, a fraction of a screen height) and `overview_zoom` (0.5, clamped\n  0.05–0.75). **Not constants in `expose.rs`** — Antonio rejected that explicitly.\n- `center_focused_column` was already fully implemented in `heca-core` and merely unreachable. Now\n  wired: `[settings] center_focused_column = \"never\" | \"on_overflow\" | \"always\"`, **default `never`\n  (niri's)**, was `OnOverflow`. Because the map draws each row at that workspace's own `view_offset`,\n  the setting shows through the map with no code in `expose.rs`.\n- Panes in a column use `Spacing::Sm` between them (at this zoom the real gap is a hairline and\n  three stacked panes read as one striped box).\n- Frosted backdrop: the layer declares `LayerBackdrop::Frosted`; the renderer runs one blur pass\n  over the scene between the chrome pass and the layer pass. Strength is the theme's\n  `overlay_frost_radius` (24 logical px). **Not `appearance.blur`** — that knob's contract is \"every\n  appearance default is off\", and three config tests enforce it.\n- Dissolve on close: `Fade` on the layer, 0.14s.\n- Eased scroll: `Eased`, τ = 0.09s.\n\n### Framework bugs found and fixed (these are the important part)\n\n**1. Seven widgets hand-rolled raw-key activation.** `Row`, `Button`, `IconButton`, `BadgeButton`,\n`Checkbox`, `Choice`, `Item` each claimed `Enter`/`Space` in the **capture** phase with no focus\ncheck. Capture runs top-down, so in any list the first one reached ate the key and returned\n`Handled::Yes`, stopping the walk before `Keymap::dispatch` could offer the resolved `Activate`\nintent. **That is why the exposé's Enter did nothing while the mouse worked.**\nFixed in `component::dispatch`: `deaf_to_raw_key` — a raw key may not be *claimed in capture* by a\nwidget that does not own the keyboard. Two owners: `Base::focused`, or `Component::takes_raw_keys()`\nwhich **defaults to `routes_own_subtree()`** (a widget routing for its children owns their keyboard).\n`Input` overrides it to `true`. All seven guards are gone. Capture-only on purpose: a container\nforwarding to its subtree still sees keys on the way back up.\n\n**2. `Dialog::submit` synthesised `Event::Key { Enter }`** at its primary button, because there was\nno way to say \"activate this child\" through `dyn Component`. Added `Component::activate()` — the\n`button.click()` that was missing. `Button::fire()` is now the one path for pointer, key and\n`activate`. Antonio: *\"i really don't understand what the problem is with dispatching an action\"* —\nthere wasn't one; I had never provided a way to.\n\n**3. The exposé blocked its own focus.** `content_covered()` was `covers_content || modal`, and the\nexposé needs `modal` to receive keys (`top_modal_root_mut`), so it could not describe itself. That\nput the app in `Domain::Overlay`, where `FocusPane` is refused — the router rejected the focus the\nmap was asking for. **Below the `Modal` band, coverage is now `covers_content` alone**; `Modal`-band\nlayers still cover unconditionally so a dialog cannot get it wrong. The exposé registers\n`modal: true, covers_content: false`. A dialog covers; a map does not.\n\n**4. The keyboard did not follow the focus.** `focus_pane` deliberately changes which pane is active\nand *nothing else* (a peek focuses without leaving). The sidebar dispatches `focus_pane` **and**\n`unfocus_dock` (`providers/workspaces/mod.rs:466`). The map now sends\n`FocusPaneThenAction { pane_id, action: UnfocusDock }` then `ActivateAction(CloseOverlay)`.\n⚠️ Antonio is right that this is still wrong: *\"not only the surface but RPC, widgets… We need a\nsingle action that does that.\"* An `activate_pane` action (focus + release whoever holds the\nkeyboard) should exist so no caller composes it by hand. **Not built. Ask before choosing between\ngiving `focus_pane` that behaviour and adding `activate_pane` beside it.**\n\n**5. The right-click menu never opened on a workspace row.** `nav_key_at` (heca-grid-ui/src/nav.rs:70)\nreads `Base::nav_key` and nothing else. Pane cards (`:944`) and columns (`:1032`) declare it; the\nworkspace `DockFrame` pushed its key into `signals.row_nav` and never told the widget. Fixed by\nadding `dock.nav_key(workspace_nav_key(ws_idx))`. **This is the bug that motivated T394** — the menu\nexisted, the mapping existed, the items existed, and one missing declaration produced silence.\n\n**6. An overlay swallowed keys it ignored.** `app/events.rs` returned unconditionally after offering\na key to the top modal layer, so anything the surface had no use for died there — which is why `q`,\ncatalogued and bound to `close_overlay` beside `Escape`, did nothing while the map was up (`Escape`\nresolves to the `dismiss` widget intent and *was* handled). It now only consumes what was handled.\n\n### Widget capabilities added (all generic, all in grid-ui)\n\n- `ScrollRegion::reveal_align(RevealAlign::{Minimal, Center})` + `center_on` — works on **both**\n  axes; `ensure_visible` was vertical-only, so a horizontal strip could never follow its cursor.\n- `ScrollRegion::overscroll(bool)` — the view may pass the ends of its content, so a centred target\n  reaches the middle even at the first/last item.\n- `ScrollRegion::scrollbars(bool)` — removes the thumb **and** its reserved gutter.\n- `ScrollRegion::smooth_scroll(secs)` — eased; a **pointer drag** snaps (it must track the finger),\n  a **wheel notch** eases (it is a discrete tenth-of-a-viewport step; applying it instantly is a\n  jump, and a run of them is a run of jumps).\n- `effects::Eased` and `effects::Fade` — in `effects.rs` beside `Flash`/`Attention`, which is where\n  Antonio said they belong. I had first inlined the same maths in `ScrollRegion` and hand-rolled a\n  third copy as a countdown in `LayerRegistry`; he called that out.\n- `PaintCx::with_opacity(alpha, f)` — multiplicative, scales every colour a context emits through\n  one `emit()` chokepoint. `fade_command` dims fill/border/glow/shadow separately.\n- `CardGrid::on_move`, `GridCell::hovered` (hover **moves** the cursor rather than raising a second\n  claim beside it), per-row `(column, cell)` memory, and vertical nav that falls through at a\n  column's ends and enters the next column at the edge you arrived from.\n- `Row::hovered()` is public.\n\n### Layers\n\n`LayerBackdrop::{Plain, Frosted}`, `Fade` on the layer, `DynamicLayer::is_active()` (visible **and**\nnot dissolving) gating coverage / top-modal / input, `remove()` waiting for the dissolve (`doomed`),\n`LayerRegistry::tick`, `frost_opacity()`.\n⚠️ **Adding the fade broke activation once**: a dissolving layer still reported `visible`, so it kept\ncovering the panes for 140ms and `FocusPane` was refused — `[heca] interaction: blocked intent from\nKeyboard`, three times. `is_active()` is the fix. An exit animation must never let a surface hold\nonto input it has already given up.\n\n### AppState\n\n`expose_cursor_per_ws: Vec<Option<PaneId>>` — the map's own highlight, per workspace, maintained\nbeside `last_visited_pane_per_ws` (grown on add, removed on delete, in the same three places).\nDeliberately **not** `last_visited_pane_per_ws`: moving a highlight around a map is *looking*, not\ngoing, and must not rewrite the focus history `prefix+i` and the sidebar's dim highlight read.\nWritten by `InteractionIntent::ExposeCursor { pane_id }` (allowed in every domain — it touches no\nsession state, and the only time it can fire is while the map is up).\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 Still open\n\n1. **T394** — the whole event vocabulary. See above.\n2. **`activate_pane`** — one action so no caller composes focus + release by hand (item 4 above).\n3. **`x` / `X` / `d` to delete a pane / column / workspace from the map.** Never built. The old\n   handoff said it needs an \"the overlay initiated it\" `ActionPolicy` arm and to **ask Antonio\n   first** — but with decision 3 above (the map no longer declares coverage) that may now be\n   unnecessary. Check before proposing a new policy variant.\n4. **Zoom in/out on open/close instead of the fade.** Antonio: *\"The animation in niri is zoom-in/out\n   not fade.\"* niri animates `zoom` from 1.0 (life size) down to 0.5. `PaintCx` has translate, clip\n   and opacity through one chokepoint, so a scale can ride the same path — but it must also scale\n   font sizes, radii and border widths. The `Fade` stays until then.\n5. **Floating panes are modelled but not drawn.** `ExposeFloating` carries strip coordinates.\n6. **`preferred_height` is ignored** — panes take an equal share of their column.\n7. **Hover border on `Row`** — it has a hover *tint* but no distinct border. Belongs in grid-ui, not\n   the exposé.\n\n## Traps this session paid for — do not re-learn them\n\n- **`view_offset` is measured from the ACTIVE COLUMN, not the strip.** The viewport's strip position\n  is `view_pos()` = `column_x(active) + view_offset`. Reading the raw offset put the workspace\n  rectangle in the wrong place in every scrolled workspace. The float test hid it by standing on\n  column 0, where the two coincide; it now stands on column 1.\n- **An `Overlay` paints its whole panel into the scene's OVERLAY layer**, so its *base* layer is\n  empty. Gating the layer render pass on \"did the base layer draw anything\" skipped it entirely and\n  `prefix+Tab` showed nothing.\n- **Bounding two numbers separately does not bound their sum.** The map's position is the centring\n  pad plus the scroll offset; bounding each let them add up to pushing everything off screen —\n  twice. `clamp_visible` now clamps the **final shift** so a quarter of the viewport's worth of\n  content always stays on screen.\n- **`grow` and `align_self` are different axes.** The strip needs `grow(1.0)` for the row's height\n  and `align_self(Start)` for its width (so it measures its columns and the region has slack).\n  Carrying a wrapper's values down left the cards **7px tall**; taking the grow away collapsed them.\n- **`Length::Pct` inside a `ScrollRegion` can never overflow it**, so nothing scrolls.\n- **`flex_grow` does not divide a region** — a share is grow + a zero base size + `shrink`.\n- **A share always fills**, so sizing columns as shares made every workspace look equally full.\n  Sizes are real size × zoom.\n- **The layer must be rebuilt before showing** (`chrome::rebuild_named_layer`): content is\n  structural; a signal replaces a prop, never a child.\n- **heca's window colour is translucent by design** (frosted compositor) — an overlay painted with it\n  lets the app read straight through.\n\n## How Antonio works — read before writing a line\n\n- **He is discussing, not commissioning, until he says otherwise.** *\"when I ask to start a\n  discussion YOU DON'T HAVE TO WRITE.\"* Answer the question; wait for \"fix\"/\"go\"/\"implement\".\n- **Answer, don't narrate.** *\"tell me the ActionPolicy is blocking instead of writing tons of\n  ceremony.\"* Short, direct, then stop.\n- **Never commit unless asked.**\n- **PRE-FLIGHT before EVERY new UI type**, not once per task: which existing widget does this; if\n  none, widget (grid-ui) or component (`heca/src/components/`); which planner task covers it. I\n  skipped it before inlining the easing and paid for it.\n- **N copies of a rule = a missing API. Fix the model, not the call site.** He rejected a hand-rolled\n  guard outright and made me move it into `dispatch`.\n- **`heca-grid-ui` must not learn about the app.** Not `ViewNode`, not `AppState`, not `WmAction`.\n- **Use the existing policy/config systems; never hardcode.** He rejected `const ZOOM` beside\n  `LayoutOptions.overview_scale`.\n- **He drives every visual check and finds what tests cannot.** Green tests found none of this\n  session's six regressions; his screenshots found all of them. **Do not claim it works.** When\n  stuck, make the code tell you — a headless dispatch test proved the exposé tree was fine and moved\n  the hunt to the app; one trace line showed the focus was already landing. Reach for those *first*,\n  not after three speculative fixes.\n- Plain English, no ceremony, no empty acknowledgements. Never mention context budget in any form.\n",
